=== Symbolic quartic factorization for cross-curve image ===

Setup: (x, y) on E_PCP(q) with y^2 = x(x+1)(x+q^2).
c = 2qy/(q^2 - x^2).
The image curve E_PCP(c) has parameter c.
A point (X, Y) on E_PCP(c) maps back via 2cY/(c^2-X^2) = q.
This gives Y = q(c^2 - X^2)/(2c) and X satisfies the quartic:
  q^2(c^2-X^2)^2 = 4c^2 X(X+1)(X+c^2).

Test point: q=20/21 x=-45/49 y=10/343 c=48/55
Roots:
[25*X + 24, 1; 121*X - 600, 1; 121*X + 96, 1; 625*X - 96, 1]
  X=-24/25  =>  Y = q(c^2 - X^2)/(2c) = -24/275
  X=600/121  =>  Y = q(c^2 - X^2)/(2c) = -17304/1331
  X=-96/121  =>  Y = q(c^2 - X^2)/(2c) = 96/1331
  X=96/625  =>  Y = q(c^2 - X^2)/(2c) = 69216/171875

